Z||000000||87ECO5||04-18-2000||08:00 PM||||Sorry to waste the space ... just had to rejoice.<P>It was a good day for the Fiero.  I had acquired a short shifter from <B>fierodave</B> and got it installed today.  <B>IT IS AWESOME!!!!!</B>  Thanks, FD!  It was great doing business with you and the shifter is FANTASTIC!  I also got my emergency brake problem fixed.  Thanks to the folks that helped out with that.  I received some components and instructions from my good friend <B>fiero56</B> that will allow me to install a manual fan switch.  And my Fiero suede ball cap arrived from the Fiero Store!<P>Now, if that guy would just send me my white face gauge decals!<P>It was a good day!  Thanks for the space ...<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 04-19-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||fiero56||04-18-2000||08:29 PM||||It was an ok day for my Fiero. I didn't do anything, but drive it to school and around town. I did see an '84 with both lights up and off on the highway, and saw a red aero-notchback parked in a lot off I-75 in West Carrollton. Looked good. I also met a Fiero guy at a local car dealership. <BR>The guy, probly in his early twenties CLAIMS, he has a super H.O. 2.8 putting out 300hp at the flywheel. I asked what he did to make that much power and he just talked about porting, and such, nothing about superchargers or anything. Says it has a 4-speed auto and can't spin the wheels. Thats when I really started to question the statements validity. I did get more information about the Fiero Enthusiasts of Dayton from him though.||||reg||1
